# Nothing here is required.
#
# The panel is served by the same binary that serves the API, so every request
# is same-origin and there is no base URL to configure. This exists for a Vite
# development server pointed at a backend somewhere else — and even then the
# proxy in vite.config.ts is the better answer, because the session cookie is
# SameSite=Lax and a cross-origin dev server would not get it.
#
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# What used to be here: VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. The
# browser talked to Supabase directly for sign-in, sign-up and password
# recovery. It talks to /api/v1/auth now, and there is no third party to hand a
# publishable key to.
